        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="1135" n="1119" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg1119"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On November 11, Admiral Joy issued a statement to the press the text of which is
                    printed in the Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>,
                    December 24, 1951, page 1035. In support of the United Nations Command position,
                    Admiral Joy asserted that the goals of the delegation were to establish a
                    demilitarized zone reflecting the military situation on the day the armistice
                    was signed; to provide adequate security for the United Nations forces, front
                    and rear, during the suspension of hostilities; to insure against a military
                    buildup beyond the level existing at the time of the armistice; and to arrive at
                    quick and satisfactory arrangements on prisoners of war. The enemy, he said,
                    wanted a <pb facs="1136" n="1120" xml:id="pg1120"/> finalized zone determined
                    immediately primarily in order to secure relief from United Nations Command
                    military pressure during a <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> cease-fire,
                    meanwhile prolonging the negotiations without cost to himself.</p>
            </div>
